<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bauto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 385</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Flavius Bauto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bauto was a Frankish general who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> as commander of the western army under Gratian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valentinian-ii">Valentinian II</a> and was consul in 385. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aelia-eudoxia">Aelia Eudoxia</a> married the eastern emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadius">Arcadius</a>, making Bauto the grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-ii">Theodosius II</a>. He is a leading example of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a> who rose to high command in the late Roman army.</p></div>
